{"name":"Hanoi","slug":"hanoi","region":"Southeast Asia & Oceania","lat":21.03,"lon":105.85,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Hanoi has warmed by about 0.15 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.1 °C in all. There is a clear El Niño signal on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 50% of a normal year-to-year swing, a noticeable tilt, though ordinary variability can easily outweigh it, roughly as much warmth as 31 years of the long-term trend. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 1.6 °C, against 0.5 °C for the coldest days. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is substantial. Rainfall shows no clear trend or El Niño link. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season has about even odds (about 55%), about 0.7 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a more humid season than normal is likely (about 75% chance). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":17.8419,"trend_per_decade":0.1507,"trend_p":0.007,"trend_total_since_1951":1.1306,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3285,"enso_p":0.0116,"confidence":"Clear","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0852,"intrinsic_sd":1.0086,"effect_this_season":0.4651,"effect_ratio":0.4611,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.715,"forecast_mean":18.5569,"forecast_sd":1.0693,"p_below":0.1672,"p_near":0.2975,"p_above":0.5354,"forecast_words":"About even odds (54%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.1838,"shrink_factor":0.5596,"effect_this_season_raw":0.831,"trend_part_2027":0.2499,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":30.8506,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.2082,"trend_p":0.0024,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2054,"enso_p":0.0777,"confidence":"Suggestive","shift_this_season":0.5196,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1344,"trend_p":0.0254,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.225,"enso_p":0.23,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.5693,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.1703,"trend_p":0.0044,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.6422,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":1.6247,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":0.4368,"enso_difference_p":0.0069,"trend_difference":-0.0379,"trend_difference_p":0.6492}},"values":[17.131,18.974,16.974,18.995,16.941,17.435,16.286,16.848,17.642,18.169,16.484,16.844,16.234,16.641,17.381,17.861,16.149,15.274,19.187,17.393,16.82,17.458,18.384,16.258,17.761,16.363,15.315,17.492,19.066,17.771,17.994,17.321,15.554,15.044,16.601,16.993,19.743,17.003,16.902,17.864,18.751,17.176,18.047,18.042,17.