n Hanoi has warmed by about 0.1 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 0.6 °C in all. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Mar–May tends to run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 10% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 70% of a normal year-to-year swing. Without El Niño, a Mar–May this warm would come about once every 4 years. Rainfall and humidity show no clear trend or El Niño link. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 75% chance), about 0.8 °C above the 1991–2020 average. The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":24.6595,"trend_per_decade":0.0847,"trend_p":0.0332,"trend_total_since_1951":0.6352,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2786,"enso_p":0.0031,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.1149,"intrinsic_sd":0.7246,"effect_this_season":0.5151,"effect_ratio":0.7109,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":4,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.7797,"forecast_mean":25.4392,"forecast_sd":0.776,"p_below":0.0827,"p_near":0.1505,"p_above":0.7668,"forecast_words":"Likely (77%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.2036,"shrink_factor":0.7309,"effect_this_season_raw":0.7048,"trend_part_2027":0.2646,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":60.8218,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1801,"trend_p":0.0892,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1866,"enso_p":0.4001,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.4722,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.0902,"trend_p":0.0051,"enso_effec